# What the sdist carries beyond setuptools' defaults (the Python package under
# src/, README.md, pyproject.toml and the license files).
#
# The Rust crate is in the sdist even though installing the sdist never builds
# it: the sdist is then a complete source release, and a downstream packager
# (conda-forge, a distro, a site build) can produce the extension from it with
#     tar xf ds42-<v>.tar.gz && cd ds42-<v> && maturin build --release
# using the [tool.maturin] table in pyproject.toml, or with rust/build.sh.
#
# scripts/fetch_digest2_model.py is included for the same reason: it resolves
# its destination relative to itself, so `python scripts/fetch_digest2_model.py`
# populates data/ inside an unpacked sdist and the test suite can then run.
#
# Deliberately NOT in the sdist:
#   * data/  -- digest2.model.csv is ~4 MB of MPC data fetched at first use by
#     scripts/fetch_digest2_model.py, is gitignored, and is not ours to
#     redistribute;
#   * validation/, paper/, docs of record, .github/ -- development material,
#     not part of the installable package;
#   * rust/target/ and any compiled extension -- build products.
# The release workflow asserts each of those absences on the built sdist rather
# than trusting these rules.

recursive-include rust *.rs *.toml *.lock *.sh *.py *.md
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include scripts *.py
include MANIFEST.in

prune rust/target
prune data
prune validation
prune paper
